# apps/web-next/.env.example
# Copy to apps/web-next/.env and edit.

# Telegram Login Widget bot @handle (NOT the secret bot token).
# The bot username is public — it is the @handle users see in Telegram.
# Set this to enable the "Sign in with Telegram" button on /auth/sign-in.
# Leave blank to hide the Telegram sign-in option (safe default for local dev
# without a registered bot).
TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=

# FR-CMS-009 — public, BROWSER-FACING Directus origin.
#
# This is the origin baked into URLs that a visitor's browser must be able to
# resolve — e.g. the source-document download links on /rules/<slug>. It is
# read at SSR runtime from process.env, so changing it needs only a restart,
# no image rebuild.
#
# Distinct from INTERNAL_DIRECTUS_URL: that one is the server-to-server base
# used for SSR fetches (a Docker-network alias such as http://directus:8055 or
# a loopback port) and is never emitted into HTML. Do not conflate them —
# putting an internal alias here produces links that DNS-fail for every real
# visitor.
#
# Use an https:// origin in any environment served over HTTPS; a plaintext
# http:// value is a mixed-content downgrade the browser may block. No trailing
# slash.
#
# Leave blank/unset to use the production default, https://cms.aiqadam.org.
PUBLIC_DIRECTUS_URL=
